{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next","id":1345858,"title":"What do we want next?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-04T13:00:27-08:00","id":1345858,"title":"What do we want next?","content":"What it says on the tin. Do we want the next Trinity release to be the 1920s-30's setting (Adventure!), a Time War, a far future setting, and ancient past setting, an Historical? What do we want? I've got my copy of the Core Book and Aeon, and I'm signed up and paid up for Aberrant. What do we want to be next in the pipe.<br /> <br /> Myself, either Adventure!, a far future ( maybe Vega is the pole star as it would be in 14,000AD), or a Time War, would be cool.<br /> <br /> Now tell us your hopes and desires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:04:19-08:00","id":1345861,"title":"","content":"Adventure! I\u2019ve never played any of them, but from reading them Adventure! is definitely my fave.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re also doing a cyberpunk game and a game based on Greek mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:20:29-08:00","id":1345864,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean, Adventure! Is next. It\u2019s already being written.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure Ian has said that Anima (2080s cyberpunk) is after that, but I\u2019m not 100%.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T13:54:04-08:00","id":1345874,"title":"","content":"Adventure! isn't being written quite yet; we're assigning writers. But yes, that's the next major book.<br /> <br /> Otherwise we haven't really said which will be &quot;next,&quot; just that there's a bunch we're considering. We have clearer ideas for some than others, so those will probably come earlier.<br /> <br /> Other eras in the primary timeline:<ul><li>\u00c6gis: Ancient Greek. psychomorphs as sorcerers, Talents as Heroes, eximorphs as gods.</li> <li>???</li> <li>Adventure!: Two-fisted pulp action and tales of derring-do.</li> <li>???</li> <li>Trinity Continuum: Modern day</li> <li>Aberrant: 2028 superheroes</li> <li>Anima: 2084, brainjack implants and the consequences thereof</li> <li>\u00c6on: 2123. Sci-fi psions</li> <li>???</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T14:22:53-08:00","id":1345892,"title":"","content":"What I want most is money so I can afford all this stuff.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, this is amazing. I didn't realize you'd actually decided two of the other eras already. This is the first game line in a very long time where I've felt like I just wanted to make sure I got everything for it, so thanks for that. I know I've been gushing about Trinity a lot but it brought me out of a serious burnout with gaming and I'm just super-impressed with the writing so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T17:08:56-08:00","id":1345953,"title":"","content":"I want the Tier 3 Paramorphs game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:05:44-08:00","id":1345970,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m going out on a limb and guessing Victorian for the era before Adventure! and Noir for the era after it.<br /> <br /> What I want most (other than the Nexus to open up to support alternate timeline settings), is a supplement after Adventure! under someone qualified like Mendez to explore Wuxia, its place in pulp, and deconstructing yellow peril and other orientalist tropes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:25:50-08:00","id":1345978,"title":"","content":"I also think they should do Victorian (like League of Extraordinary Gentlemen) and maybe a space opera game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:47:46-08:00","id":1345992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1345978#post1345978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think they should do Victorian (like League of Extraordinary Gentlemen) and maybe a space opera game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah what\u2019s already hinted at in the Fate of Humanity chapter in Aeon makes clear what follows is a far flung space opera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T18:49:37-08:00","id":1345993,"title":"","content":"Cool. I love space opera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T19:17:36-08:00","id":1345999,"title":"","content":"Soooooo many options, which I love. I honestly look forward to any of the books that they create in the Trinity Continuum. I also really hope every one they do is more successful then they expected so they can always make more.<br /> <br /> First, I am really looking forward to Adventure! It deserves to be brought back and given love. <br /> <br /> The Aegis setting sounds cool, especially as that will be a bit 'fantasy' like, which would take the TC rules in a brilliant direction. <br /> <br /> The space opera setting is also really cool as well. Related to this is seeing how they would update and modify the current Psi powers to give the feel of human evolution making us improved. <br /> <br /> As I go through the Trinity Core book and read the Gifts of the Talents a tier 3 game of them would be brilliant. As was mentioned I figure their Gifts would in some ways be like the Charms of the Solar Exalted and that would be EPIC!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T22:21:46-08:00","id":1346058,"title":"","content":"Though I don't expect it, it'd be neat to see a 1950s atomic horror core book that has rules for They Came From Beneath The Sea crossover campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-04T23:26:21-08:00","id":1346078,"title":"","content":"In <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4\" data-vbnamecard=\"4\">IanWatson</a>'s outline above, there's an unnamed era sandwiched between TC:Adventure! and TC:modern; it's <i>possible</i> that that might be TC:Atomic. I certainly wouldn't mind if it is. <br /> <br /> I'm also hoping that one of the things that TC:Anima does is to introduce the possibility of sentient machines into the setting: primitive, unreliable, and dangerous machines that get banned along with the rest of the brain-interface hardtech of the era when it's over; but present nonetheless. <br /> <br /> Then, with the space opera era, I'd like to see them return in a more stable form, possibly as the successors to an alien species that took the route briefly explored by TC:Anima to its conclusion and have transitioned to a society of machines. Humanity, of course, would still be human (or parahuman, in the case of the Quantum-powered ones); but psiads and parahumans would both have evolved (I see most parahumans being similar to TC:\u00c6's Superiors, but with a wider variety of powers that include something like TC:Ab's Body Modification), and even Talents might end up with a few new tricks up their sleeves (Exalted in Space, anyone?). <br /> <br /> As to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a>'s request for a Wuxia element: I'd put that as a divergent era (similar to how the modern era is divergent from the TC:A!/TC:Ab/TC:\u00c6 sequence) or a historical era (similar to \u00c6gis, but set in historical China), and I'd have it be the result of a localized Event that's focused on Flux and results in Tier 3 Talents \u2014 thus, Wuxia. <br /> <br /> Finally, I'd really like to see a time- and dimension-hopping \u201csetting\u201d with a focus on Tier 4 Talents (with Tier 4 being when they unlock their full potential to manipulate time and space, and thus to become Travelers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T00:53:06-08:00","id":1346093,"title":"","content":"Also, does anyone else think its funny that the most common running theme of the Trinity setting is &quot;okay, bad idea, don't try that again!&quot; I'm not sure if any human decisions ended the Adventure! era, but Aberrant ends with &quot;okay, those were a bad idea&quot; and Anima ends with, &quot;okay, brain tech was a bad idea&quot; and Aeon is already in the middle of &quot;maybe psions are actually a bad idea&quot; (with the Quantakinetic purge and the shift away from relying on teleporters.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T01:14:31-08:00","id":1346100,"title":"","content":"Personally, the 3 question marks Ian left I would make:<br /> The first around the Discovery/Colonisation of the American Continent, El Dorado stuff (Victorian and pulp are really connected, Victorian being the inspiration to pulp)<br /> The second I would put on a 70\u2019s 80\u2019s stile, with the surge of low level novas Psiads and talents working as super-soldiers and super-spies on the Cold War (noir is basically pulp but darker).<br /> The third I would make a Space Opera on Star Trek TOS stile, finding ancient gods living in space and sexy aliens fighting in colosseum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T02:09:29-08:00","id":1346103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346093#post1346093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, does anyone else think its funny that the most common running theme of the Trinity setting is &quot;okay, bad idea, don't try that again!&quot; I'm not sure if any human decisions ended the Adventure! era, but Aberrant ends with &quot;okay, those were a bad idea&quot; and Anima ends with, &quot;okay, brain tech was a bad idea&quot; and Aeon is already in the middle of &quot;maybe psions are actually a bad idea&quot; (with the Quantakinetic purge and the shift away from relying on teleporters.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm\u2026 kind of. From the future history we're given in the back of TC:\u00c6, it's eventually discovered that psions are the result of malicious alien meddling, with psiads being humanity's true psionic heritage. But there's not really a backlash against psions: if anything, they tend to be seen as fellow victims of the Doyen manipulations: after all, the Prometheus Chambers artificially limited their potential. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346100#post1346100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, the 3 question marks Ian left I would make:<br /> The first around the Discovery/Colonisation of the American Continent, El Dorado stuff (Victorian and pulp are really connected, Victorian being the inspiration to pulp)</div> </div> </div> </div> Nitpick: Discovery and colonization of the American Continents was late 1400s to early 1700s; the Victorian era was the mid-to-late 1800s. They're distinct eras. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346100#post1346100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second I would put on a 70\u2019s 80\u2019s style, with the surge of low level novas Psiads and talents working as super-soldiers and super-spies on the Cold War (noir is basically pulp but darker).</div> </div> </div> </div> Recall that during this time, the Doyen had erected a barrier around the Earth that suppressed the likes of Hammersmith Events; when Divas Mal triggered the Galatea Event, a case could be made that it was as potent as it was because it needed to be in order to shatter the Doyen barrier. But that does mean that the Cold War would have been a period of waning power where Stalwarts and Mesmerists are concerned: it would likely have been an all-Talents era. That said, I could also see something triggered by Roswell, with the trigger being the crash-landed of an alien spacecraft whose detonated drive system serves like a localized Hammersmith Event. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346100#post1346100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The third I would make a Space Opera on Star Trek TOS style, finding ancient gods living in space and sexy aliens fighting in colosseum.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to lean more toward classic Legion of Superheroes (for that era's Quantum-powered types) or Lensman (for that era's Psi-powered types), supplemented by a small selection of aliens and robots. In particular, the humanoid \u201caliens\u201d (the ones who seem mostly human save for a few cosmetic differences like pigmentation or bumpy foreheads) would mostly have started out as \u00c6on or post-\u00c6on Aberrant cults before developing into stable parahuman space cultures over the intervening centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-05-2019, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T04:21:01-08:00","id":1346123,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> what\u2019s a Traveler?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T05:07:27-08:00","id":1346129,"title":"","content":"Personally I\u2019d love to see what they had planned for the far future space opera supplement, also a book about the cybertech of the aberrant era would be nice, pitting cyber enhanced baselines against novas would be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5811-starkiller","name":"Starkiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T05:32:38-08:00","id":1346135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346123#post1346123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> what\u2019s a Traveler?</div> </div> </div> </div>A term I coined just now: a Talent with the power to manipulate time and space, and thus to be able to travel across time and space. Max Mercer would be a Traveler; in fact, thus far, he's the only known Traveler.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T06:47:57-08:00","id":1346147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1345874#post1345874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adventure! isn't being written quite yet; we're assigning writers. But yes, that's the next major book.<br /> <br /> Otherwise we haven't really said which will be &amp;quot;next,&amp;quot; just that there's a bunch we're considering. We have clearer ideas for some than others, so those will probably come earlier.<br /> <br /> Other eras in the primary timeline:<ul><li>\u00c6gis: Ancient Greek. psychomorphs as sorcerers, Talents as Heroes, eximorphs as gods.</li> <li>???</li> <li>Adventure!: Two-fisted pulp action and tales of derring-do.</li> <li>???</li> <li>Trinity Continuum: Modern day</li> <li>Aberrant: 2028 superheroes</li> <li>Anima: 2084, brainjack implants and the consequences thereof</li> <li>\u00c6on: 2123. Sci-fi psions</li> <li>???</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* it said first draft so I guessed.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if the next one isn\u2019t decided next, then I personally really hope it\u2019s Aegis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T08:01:18-08:00","id":1346162,"title":"","content":"Just for a matter of explaining, I was explaining why not Victorian and why not Noir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T08:31:44-08:00","id":1346165,"title":"","content":"Ah! That clarifies things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T08:57:18-08:00","id":1346170,"title":"","content":"Fingers crossed for Aegis; I\u2019m especially keen to see all three types in a single setting and rule set, as Aberrant seems like something of an outlier rules wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3631-adamrice","name":"AdamRice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:02:13-08:00","id":1346172,"title":"","content":"You'll be getting the three-in-one setting with TC:A!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:36:14-08:00","id":1346185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346058#post1346058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I don't expect it, it'd be neat to see a 1950s atomic horror core book that has rules for They Came From Beneath The Sea crossover campaigns.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's something I was considering... and then They Came from Beneath the Sea! was announced.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want to have two games out covering the same territory. It's an idea we might return to in the future, but only after TCfBtS has had a chance to firmly establish itself. It's not even out yet.<br /> <br /> So no, it's not that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T09:52:15-08:00","id":1346190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346172#post1346172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll be getting the three-in-one setting with TC:A!</div> </div> </div> </div>True enough; my hope is that Aegis is a little higher powered on the Nova end, as I would I\u2019m assuming Adventure! will have Stalwarts similar to Superiors, which are terrific but not as high powered as I would like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3631-adamrice","name":"AdamRice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T10:01:19-08:00","id":1346194,"title":"","content":"I really liked the idea of Trinity Aegis. It is one era that could be awesome to use or be inspired. I was already thinking about how to adapt themes and portions of Eberron and Iron Kingdoms, and with a sourcebook to have as refference would be great.<br /> <br /> Other things that would be awesome is if there was a book with details on how the writers create the quantum powers, psions, and any traits from all eras so people who wants to add new rules or want to use the rules in different settings can get an idea in how to use the mechanics. Some kind of guide to house rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","user":"Oxcelot","date":". 11-05-2019, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23839-oxcelot","name":"Oxcelot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:02:23-08:00","id":1346213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346100#post1346100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, the 3 question marks Ian left I would make:<br /> The first around the Discovery/Colonisation of the American Continent, El Dorado stuff (Victorian and pulp are really connected, Victorian being the inspiration to pulp)</div> </div> </div> </div>if this is set in the main timeline, and thus shaped like real world history, I have no idea how they could separate that from \u201clet\u2019s play genocide!\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T11:07:09-08:00","id":1346215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1345874#post1345874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]\u00c6gis: Ancient Greek. psychomorphs as sorcerers, Talents as Heroes, eximorphs as gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>i would think heroes in the Greek Myth sense would be eximorphs. The difference between them and the gods being degree more than type.<br /> <br /> something like...<br /> <br /> Gods: Novas<br /> Demigod Heroes: Stalwarts<br /> Oracles, Witches, other Mystics: Mesmerists<br /> Mortals who Cool Stuff Happens Around: Talents","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T12:46:41-08:00","id":1346245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346213#post1346213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> if this is set in the main timeline, and thus shaped like real world history, I have no idea how they could separate that from \u201clet\u2019s play genocide!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Plague Inc Renascence Edition! There are the symptoms, but also the conquerors (one tab just for Conquerors qualities).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T16:34:51-08:00","id":1346315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346215#post1346215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i would think heroes in the Greek Myth sense would be eximorphs. The difference between them and the gods being degree more than type.<br /> <br /> something like...<br /> <br /> Gods: Novas<br /> Demigod Heroes: Stalwarts<br /> Oracles, Witches, other Mystics: Mesmerists<br /> Mortals who Cool Stuff Happens Around: Talents</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Per Adventure! 1st Edition, page 27:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>From the Journal of Doctor Primoris - April 24 1924</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we can look to myth and legend for a different way to categorize the new breed walking the earth, should categories be desired. Daredevils are the heroes of myth, the Daedaluses as well as the Jasons. Mesmerists are the wizards, witches and sorcerers who haunt the corners of our past. And stalwarts? Stalwarts are gods. Gods of the dawning age.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're following that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T16:55:47-08:00","id":1346318,"title":"","content":"If the non-linear time element in Mummy The Curse 2e gains a lot of positive feedback maybe we could see something like that in Trinity. I mean, after all, Talents at high level can get unstuck from time right and that could lead to a non-linear campaign experience. <br /> <br /> On the matter of Novas as gods I wonder if that means that might be a setting where Corruption is turned down, since the gods aren't really looked at as such (not saying they don't have their own hubris faults but them being corrupted isn't really what they are).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T19:25:28-08:00","id":1346331,"title":"","content":"If there was a 1950s sci fi thing with giant ants, Godzilla, the Fly, 50 foot womeen, creatures from the Black Lagoon, cat women from the Moon, teenaged werewolves, alien body snatchers, and robots fighting Aztec mummies, I think it should be titled ATOMICS! (Yes, all caps plus exclamation mark.)<br /> <br /> Action!, the 1970s setting of cyborgs, martial artists, streetwise detectives, and psychics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 11-05-2019, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T21:05:23-08:00","id":1346351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346078#post1346078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4\" data-vbnamecard=\"4\">IanWatson</a>'s outline above, there's an unnamed era sandwiched between TC:Adventure! and TC:modern; it's <i>possible</i> that that might be TC:Atomic. I certainly wouldn't mind if it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd love to see something in the Cold War era. Might be fun to introduce MK Ultra etc as proto-psions/second gen mesmerists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T21:08:43-08:00","id":1346352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Starkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346129#post1346129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I\u2019d love to see what they had planned for the far future space opera supplement, also a book about the cybertech of the aberrant era would be nice, pitting cyber enhanced baselines against novas would be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a big fan of the characters The Engineer (the Authority) and Bloodshot (from Valiant) and the Tony Stark's armor from Infinity War, it'd be super cool to do a cyborg variant using nanobots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T02:22:15-08:00","id":1346403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queen Anne Country</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346352#post1346352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a big fan of the characters The Engineer (the Authority) and Bloodshot (from Valiant) and the Tony Stark's armor from Infinity War, it'd be super cool to do a cyborg variant using nanobots.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are reasonably straight forward to make using the Aberrant tech rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T09:10:07-08:00","id":1346473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346403#post1346403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These are reasonably straight forward to make using the Aberrant tech rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure - haven't yet but will - however it might be neat to see them become &quot;regular&quot; tech a la VARGs in the distant space operatic future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T11:23:30-08:00","id":1346519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346315#post1346315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Per Adventure! 1st Edition, page 27:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We're following that.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the broad strokes of Eximorphs and Psychomorphs, or sticking closely to Adventure!\u2019s power level for the \u201cgods\u201d? I ask because I understood Michael as referring to what Stalwarts were the dawn of, and Nova dominance over the forces of nature would seem necessary to pull off divine miracles.<br /> <br /> Or do you marine car in a new middle path with different era appropriate Eximorph mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T12:52:38-08:00","id":1346547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346519#post1346519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In the broad strokes of Eximorphs and Psychomorphs, or sticking closely to Adventure!\u2019s power level for the \u201cgods\u201d? I ask because I understood Michael as referring to what Stalwarts were the dawn of, and Nova dominance over the forces of nature would seem necessary to pull off divine miracles.<br /> <br /> Or do you marine car in a new middle path with different era appropriate Eximorph mechanics?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you multiply any feat a Superior can do by the power of myth over a long time, you will get some great feats for sure. Add to that the possibility of \u201cQ-Tech\u201d and you get the Zeus Lightining bolt, Apollo bow and arrows, Poseidon Trident, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-06-2019, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T13:20:26-08:00","id":1346554,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I want Anima after Adventure!. \u00c6gis is cool and all; and I'm not arguing against ever publishing it. But frankly, if I want to do legendary heroes, mystics, and gods, I've got Scion. The only difference between \u00c6gis vs. Scion and 50s-era Trinity vs. They Came From Beneath the Sea is that TCFBTS is newer. I'd like to get one or two more original settings before we start dealing with settings that overlap with other Storypath gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-06-2019, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T14:06:22-08:00","id":1346569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1345953#post1345953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want the Tier 3 Paramorphs game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would be a time war game. I assume it's further down the line. But I want it too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T14:31:40-08:00","id":1346575,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think tier 4 should be where you get to the time war stuff; tier 3 ought to be now along the lines of Wuxia/Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:03:18-08:00","id":1346602,"title":"","content":"I would put Time and Dimension travel as a late tier Talent power, like the 5 dot powers for Psiads, you can reach one if you specialise. Seeing thru dimensions/Mist or time would be a easier power to get, but quite limited (like a 3 dot power for Psiads)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:18:41-08:00","id":1346607,"title":"","content":"Me, I think that actual time or dimensional travel should be more akin to the 6+-dot psion powers; and even then, they should start out as subconscious, uncontrolled, and/or unreliable: No matter how far you develop them, there should always be restrictions on how they can be used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T16:59:30-08:00","id":1346618,"title":"","content":"Crosstime Travel in the First Edition of Aberrant was one of the highest tier powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T17:54:24-08:00","id":1346628,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see Time travel setup once all 3 games are on the table I'd also like to see Tier 3 Paramorphs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T18:41:30-08:00","id":1346632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346618#post1346618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crosstime Travel in the First Edition of Aberrant was one of the highest tier powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Novas are Tier 4. All three more reason why Travelers would be tier 4, not tier 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T01:56:02-08:00","id":1346685,"title":"","content":"A time travel game would need multiple sets of time travel rules. This would reflect the simple fact that different groups have different ways to travel in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T05:51:50-08:00","id":1346702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346685#post1346685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A time travel game would need multiple sets of time travel rules. This would reflect the simple fact that different groups have different ways to travel in time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In 2e I don't think anyone has time travel ability other than Mercer right now. I could easily see them limiting time travel to Talents only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T06:13:54-08:00","id":1346707,"title":"","content":"For my part, I'd still like a hard and fast formula I could use to convert stuff (powers/skills/equipment/difficulties) from Old Trinity (including Aberrant and Adventure) into Trinity Continuum so that all that stuff we got as part of the bundles could be made relevant/usable in the new system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:48:06-08:00","id":1346798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346707#post1346707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For my part, I'd still like a hard and fast formula I could use to convert stuff (powers/skills/equipment/difficulties) from Old Trinity (including Aberrant and Adventure) into Trinity Continuum so that all that stuff we got as part of the bundles could be made relevant/usable in the new system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be something for a Player's Guide to the Core Rulebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T11:52:21-08:00","id":1346801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346702#post1346702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In 2e I don't think anyone has time travel ability other than Mercer right now. I could easily see them limiting time travel to Talents only.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you said &quot;right now.&quot; If Novas can create universes, they can time travel. It may be trickier and more complicated than how Inspired Talents do it, but if you can make your own universe with its own physical laws, you can time travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T12:19:47-08:00","id":1346816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346801#post1346801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As you said &quot;right now.&quot; If Novas can create universes, they can time travel. It may be trickier and more complicated than how Inspired Talents do it, but if you can make your own universe with its own physical laws, you can time travel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think you'll see novas with universe creation powers, unless they are the Quantum 10 ones who have transcended, and they (at least in the current draft we have access to) move on to some other kind of existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T16:11:24-08:00","id":1346887,"title":"","content":"Novas of that power level are mentioned, not described, in the secrets section of the AEON book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T16:18:39-08:00","id":1346888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346801#post1346801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As you said &quot;right now.&quot; If Novas can create universes, they can time travel. It may be trickier and more complicated than how Inspired Talents do it, but if you can make your own universe with its own physical laws, you can time travel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think that's necissarily the case? There may be all sorts of limits to what you can and can't do as a universe creator. Even 1e had all sorts of differences based on success rolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T16:57:04-08:00","id":1346894,"title":"","content":"My first view of the level 5 and 6 powers of 1e was: I want them! And: So much power is wonderful!, but honestly, it must be impossible to play it for several reasons, not just as player characters but also as adversaries (not even saying enemies). it doesn\u2019t mean I think Novas should or should not be able to time travel (in my game they would not be capable), but the presence of those powers in game as part of the rules are probably just for showing how far it can go. I honestly prefere the idea of the 11 dots in purviews from Scion 1e, your character become a unstoppable force or an unmovable object, what fits better, and you (as a player) becomes a StoryGuide for anything related to your purview.<br /> <br /> Anyway, time is not a Quantum Force, for example a Nova can manipulate gravity for reducing or increasing the speed of time, but not to make it flow back (you can question the time arrow direction in Quantum theory, but it\u2019s not part of Quantum, just a side effect of the way quantum works). A Nova would be capable of something like DR Manhattan knowing past and future as memories due to Quantum arrow direction, and possibly travel back to his past self to change past due to his capacities, but travelling time is a bit off in my view, like Telepathy and Precognition.<br /> <br /> Talents and Excelsiors (as I like to call them, RIP Stan Lee), would be capable of time manipulation, time travel and cross time travel. I would add a kind of Infinity Unprobability to allow them to teleport too... but I don\u2019t mind you not liking the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T03:29:54-08:00","id":1346968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346888#post1346888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think that's necissarily the case? There may be all sorts of limits to what you can and can't do as a universe creator. Even 1e had all sorts of differences based on success rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, once your power level gets to &quot;universe creation&quot; or &quot;human sized Death Star&quot; who gives a crap about &quot;limits?&quot; My take on that stuff was, &quot;Congratulations, you're now God. Unfortunately, in my games there's only one God and since I'm the GM, that's me. So, I'll be taking that character as an NPC now.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T05:09:21-08:00","id":1346984,"title":"","content":"We need a new thread for this time travel discussion. I assume that were time travel will be easy and natural for the highest level Inspired. I assume it will be tricky complex frustrating and very hard for Psions, Psiads, Novas, et al. It will be a matter of game balance.<br /> <br /> Now, let's talk about what games we want next and in the pipeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T06:51:48-08:00","id":1347002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1346984#post1346984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We need a new thread for this time travel discussion. I assume that were time travel will be easy and natural for the highest level Inspired. I assume it will be tricky complex frustrating and very hard for Psions, Psiads, Novas, et al. It will be a matter of game balance.<br /> <br /> Now, let's talk about what games we want next and in the pipeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we need a new thread for Time Travel because we don't need any sort of &quot;system&quot; for time travel. Systems for usage are only important for those things that are &quot;useful&quot; to PCs. Firearms. Psionic healing. Nova blasts. Piloting. Detection. Etc. You really do not want Time Travel to be &quot;useful&quot; to PCs. Because they'll use it. &quot;Yeah, since we got our asses handed to us in that fight with the Aberrant that was like a werewolf, I'm gonna time travel us all couple days back and get us some silver weapons/bullets and then we'll fight him again.&quot; or &quot;I time travel us back to make the roll again. And again. And again.&quot; And your campaign turns into a video game including a save/load game feature. And do you really want &quot;Hey, remember that time that was six months ago in real life where we turned right up that corridor? I'm gonna Time Travel us back to that point and we're gonna go left instead&quot; to be a thing that happens in your game? A lot.<br /> <br /> Time Travel needs to be a purely GM-controlled plot device. Any rolls the PCs make in conjunction with it should have all possible results fully mapped out before the dice are touched. Otherwise Time Travel should mostly be variations of &quot;The technicians flip their switches and you're surround by the green glow and hearing that boopity-boopity-boop noise. Suddenly you're in 13th century England. Oh shit, there's an Aberrant about to eat Robin of Loxley. Best get to it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 11-08-2019, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T12:31:41-08:00","id":1347080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1347002#post1347002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time Travel needs to be a purely GM-controlled plot device. Any rolls the PCs make in conjunction with it should have all possible results fully mapped out before the dice are touched. Otherwise Time Travel should mostly be variations of &quot;The technicians flip their switches and you're surround by the green glow and hearing that boopity-boopity-boop noise. Suddenly you're in 13th century England. Oh shit, there's an Aberrant about to eat Robin of Loxley. Best get to it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet, systems still count. If those sent into the past by the Psion need to avoid getting anywhere near famous and/or important people, or else (your horrid fate here) that imposes limits on their actions. If the time travelers sent by a Nova have to realize that, if they cause any change to history, they won't have a future to return to, because their future will be replaced with another one, that imposes limits on them. If time travelers sent by the Inspired are free to act because time heals itself around them so they don't need to fear random disasters, but they can still make limited changes, that frees them up. The systems of time travel dictate styles of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T15:35:54-08:00","id":1347113,"title":"","content":"Existing settings don't include time travel, save only for Max Mercer's \u201cunstuck in time\u201d time travel. A hypothetical time travel setting should take that into account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T16:28:10-08:00","id":1347124,"title":"","content":"I've been doing a lot of time travel stuff in my games, but that's been GM fiat and player suggestion and I have absolutely no idea how to mechanically quantify it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T16:40:15-08:00","id":1347127,"title":"","content":"If it is out of the players hands, it doesn't need mechanics.it is only when the players have some measure of control over it that mechanics are needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T18:16:42-08:00","id":1347149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1347080#post1347080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet, systems still count. If those sent into the past by the Psion need to avoid getting anywhere near famous and/or important people, or else (your horrid fate here) that imposes limits on their actions. If the time travelers sent by a Nova have to realize that, if they cause any change to history, they won't have a future to return to, because their future will be replaced with another one, that imposes limits on them. If time travelers sent by the Inspired are free to act because time heals itself around them so they don't need to fear random disasters, but they can still make limited changes, that frees them up. The systems of time travel dictate styles of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all fine, but that's about what happens after the Time Travel once they get whenever they're going. My point is that you don't allow the PCs to control the mechanism, the traveling part, of time travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T18:47:35-08:00","id":1347156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1347149#post1347149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's all fine, but that's about what happens after the Time Travel once they get whenever they're going. My point is that you don't allow the PCs to control the mechanism, the traveling part, of time travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you don't give them free rein to go whenever and wherever they like, with no restrictions. Imagine if you had a teleporter who could jump to anywhere in the Galaxy at whim, with no restrictions (e.g., no travel time, no way to block them or exhaust them, etc.). That would be bad. <br /> <br /> But the flip side to that is that if you're doing a time war setting and you never give them any agency in terms of when and where they end up, you will end up with some very frustrated players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T11:29:16-08:00","id":1347292,"title":"","content":"For the Aeon setting, I hope they publish an Atlas of Aeon Earth. Something to flesh out the setting and make adventures on Earth more workable. The Psi Orders need their own book as does the Aeon Foundation.<br /> <br /> The Foundations in the Core Book need their own book too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T11:34:09-08:00","id":1347296,"title":"","content":"The Early Modern/Renaissance period would be a great setting for a Talents game. Perhaps alchemists are somehow tapping into flux. Weak Psiads would be viable characters too. Some type of low level Superior/Stalwart would also be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T14:20:41-08:00","id":1347323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1347292#post1347292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Aeon setting, I hope they publish an Atlas of Aeon Earth. Something to flesh out the setting and make adventures on Earth more workable. The Psi Orders need their own book as does the Aeon Foundation.<br /> <br /> The Foundations in the Core Book need their own book too.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand, Terra Firma is all about Earth during Aeon Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T14:34:44-08:00","id":1347324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1347323#post1347323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand, Terra Firma is all about Earth during Aeon Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I didn't know that. (or maybe I did but I forgot, lol) So when it comes to Aeon besides the Core we get a book about space and a book about Earth and a book about tech/psiads/and superiors. That is a pretty awesome starting set. But even more if the other two are as good as Aeon Aexpansion then they are going to be mighty fine, mighty fine indeed. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T15:34:34-08:00","id":1347332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1347323#post1347323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I understand, Terra Firma is all about Earth during Aeon Era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Earth and Luna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T16:24:10-08:00","id":1347342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1347332#post1347332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Earth and Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Grand! I hope the maps and political details are well fleshed out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T17:18:21-08:00","id":1347348,"title":"","content":"Hmm.<br /> <br /> personal preference: Adventure!, \u00c6on, Aberrant, in that order. Then one of the new settings. <br /> <br /> For \u00c6on, a world guide, an orders guide, a tech guide, a space guide, and an antagonists guide. <br /> For Aberrant, a big collection of factions/npcs that you can mix and match as needed to create the sort of setting you want; maybe a series of them, themed after science/tech research &amp;exploration, social politics &amp; celebrity, physical conflict &amp; stryfe, crime &amp; conspiracy, and so forth. <br /> For Adventure!, a world guide that includes lost worlds and other oddities, some sort of faction guide, a pulp science tech guide, and some sort of chronicle guide that looks at running decades long games where the PCs might radically alter history.<br /> <br /> And currently pondering the idea of Aquarius, a late 60s/early to mid 70s setting involving New Age psychics, alien astronauts, and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T18:36:26-08:00","id":1347370,"title":"","content":"It might be a little too niche, but I'd love a book that covers the various Aberrant takeovers of colonies to make them playable. Like, the Space Brigard, the stuff on Alpha Centauri, etc. Being a resistance group member or a time traveling interloper in those events would be really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T18:49:35-08:00","id":1347374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1347370#post1347370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be a little too niche, but I'd love a book that covers the various Aberrant takeovers of colonies to make them playable. Like, the Space Brigard, the stuff on Alpha Centauri, etc. Being a resistance group member or a time traveling interloper in those events would be really cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea. It does add to playablity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T20:54:00-08:00","id":1347395,"title":"","content":"I would really love an Aberrant book with various alternate futures arrayed them, like the chapter of Psions in the Modern Day but more. The fact that 2e is a Continuum is great, but now I wish we would have more support for seeing that continuum in action. <br /> <br /> By the way, this could alternately be done by having another 'major' game line within the Trinity Continuum that is clearly outside of the linear timeline path of Adventure! Aberrant Aeon. Like maybe a post-modern one that is steamship and skyships or even a modern setting where Talents are basically like the Solar Exalted in terms of Gifts that become very very visible. Just sayin. <br /> <br /> That all said what I really wish was that I was rich and could say &quot;Hey Onyx Path here is a million dollars, write many more Trinity Continuum books!&quot; Alas I am not rich and thus cannot do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T12:55:48-08:00","id":1347740,"title":"","content":"One thing I would love after the the Aberrant and Far Future games are printed is a book of about five to six worked examples of worlds colonized in the 2030-2050 period. Each world should have a section on settlement, the colony's condition in 2123, and it's status in the far future. Example: Planet New Plymouth settled by warp gates created by Novas in the 2040's. Different cultural groups among the settlers feel slighted or threatened by the divisions of territory and resources. In 2123, hostilities between different language and religious groups on the main continent. The American, Irish, Welsh, Korean, and Czech, groups, settled on large islands in the southern ocean are isolationist. In the far future, a post-apocalyptic land of primitive tribes in the North. Peaceful advanced societies in the southern Ocean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T13:04:35-08:00","id":1347743,"title":"","content":"You do know that there's a book in the works right now that's essentially going to cover this, right? Not necessarily the \u201cfuture fate\u201d part; but \u201cwhat colonies are out there during the \u00c6on era\u201d part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T18:40:43-08:00","id":1347809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1347743#post1347743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know that there's a book in the works right now that's essentially going to cover this, right? Not necessarily the \u201cfuture fate\u201d part; but \u201cwhat colonies are out there during the \u00c6on era\u201d part.</div> </div> </div> </div>That I knew. It's the idea of the same worlds in three different periods I'm suggesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T13:14:20-08:00","id":1347994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next#post1345858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it says on the tin. Do we want the next Trinity release to be the 1920s-30's setting (Adventure!), a Time War, a far future setting, and ancient past setting, an Historical? What do we want? I've got my copy of the Core Book and Aeon, and I'm signed up and paid up for Aberrant. What do we want to be next in the pipe.<br /> <br /> Myself, either Adventure!, a far future ( maybe Vega is the pole star as it would be in 14,000AD), or a Time War, would be cool.<br /> <br /> Now tell us your hopes and desires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't about next, but one thing I'd like to get eventually is something that works as magic/occult. Maybe set around a prehistoric Atlantis/Hyborea/etc.<br /> <br /> One thing I plan to do when I finally put together a campaign is to incorporate the idea of Para-quantum. Aberrants/Novas use Quantum, pulling their power directly from the stuff that allows our reality to exist. Perhaps because they pull power from a reality that they're part of, they're susceptible to alteration through Corruption. Psions/Psiads use sub-quantum, somehow pulling power from below the Planck limit. Talents (unconsciously) use Flux or perhaps a better term might be sur/super-quantum, pulling energy from universes near and similar to our own. So magicians/occultists, hmm, how about Dimensioners? Dimensioners would use Paraquantum, energy, pulling power from universes accessible to but very different from our, with different physics, alien concepts even more alien beings.<br /> <br /> There wouldn't necessarily be completely unique effects for Para-quantum. There's plenty of overlap in terms of effects between the current abilities. The differences come from their trappings and associated effects. To see in the dark, a Talent might use Super-science to build special glasses; a psion/psiad might use the EK Photokinetic mode, EM Sight; a nova simply have Mega-Perception with the Enhancement, Electromagnetic Vision (or whatever the Trinity Continuum version becomes); and a Dimensioner might invoke &quot;Blindsight&quot; which causes her to see Darkness as a kind of light (while conversely seeing bright light as darkness).<br /> <br /> Para-quantum would be a way to bring in concepts from Call of Cthluhu or Dark Conspiracy. There are other worlds, other realities than this one. Some of them know about us. And they hunger. For us.<br /> <br /> Those weird things with the bug-eye that spat acid? Maybe those were just some kind of sub-aberrant mutation. But maybe they were from Somewhere Else. Plus, stuff like that gives you a way to provide situations for your Tier 3 (4?!) characters to mess with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","user":"johntfs","date":". 11-12-2019, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T17:31:28-08:00","id":1348079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1347994#post1347994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't about next, but one thing I'd like to get eventually is something that works as magic/occult. Maybe set around a prehistoric Atlantis/Hyborea/etc.<br /> <br /> One thing I plan to do when I finally put together a campaign is to incorporate the idea of Para-quantum. Aberrants/Novas use Quantum, pulling their power directly from the stuff that allows our reality to exist. Perhaps because they pull power from a reality that they're part of, they're susceptible to alteration through Corruption. Psions/Psiads use sub-quantum, somehow pulling power from below the Planck limit. Talents (unconsciously) use Flux or perhaps a better term might be sur/super-quantum, pulling energy from universes near and similar to our own. So magicians/occultists, hmm, how about Dimensioners? Dimensioners would use Paraquantum, energy, pulling power from universes accessible to but very different from our, with different physics, alien concepts even more alien beings.<br /> <br /> There wouldn't necessarily be completely unique effects for Para-quantum. There's plenty of overlap in terms of effects between the current abilities. The differences come from their trappings and associated effects. To see in the dark, a Talent might use Super-science to build special glasses; a psion/psiad might use the EK Photokinetic mode, EM Sight; a nova simply have Mega-Perception with the Enhancement, Electromagnetic Vision (or whatever the Trinity Continuum version becomes); and a Dimensioner might invoke &amp;quot;Blindsight&amp;quot; which causes her to see Darkness as a kind of light (while conversely seeing bright light as darkness).<br /> <br /> Para-quantum would be a way to bring in concepts from Call of Cthluhu or Dark Conspiracy. There are other worlds, other realities than this one. Some of them know about us. And they hunger. For us.<br /> <br /> Those weird things with the bug-eye that spat acid? Maybe those were just some kind of sub-aberrant mutation. But maybe they were from Somewhere Else. Plus, stuff like that gives you a way to provide situations for your Tier 3 (4?!) characters to mess with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Find a PDF of Eldritch Skies. It's a sci fi setting useing Lovecraft's cosmology. Even if you don't like the game, for you it will be inspirational.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T18:46:34-08:00","id":1348100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1348079#post1348079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Find a PDF of Eldritch Skies. It's a sci fi setting useing Lovecraft's cosmology. Even if you don't like the game, for you it will be inspirational.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to find it. To be fair, I don't want to specifically use Lovecraft's Mythos simply because of how over used it already is. I want to integrate cosmic horror elements into Trinity to a certain extent but I don't want it to become Cthulhu Calls to Trinity or something especially not at first. For one thing, there's plenty of cool other stuff in Trinity. For another, Trinity is about Hope and Optimism. Lovecraft's cosmology is about as hopeless/depressing as you can get. <br /> <br /> A lot of it would be hints, clues, indications. The sub-Aberrant that doesn't seem to be part of any known Aberrant. The biotech lab whose &quot;bio&quot; seems really freaky. The intternet/opnet meme that really does seem to be driving people to kill - or do other things. The Aberrant cult centered on an &quot;Aberrant&quot; nobody recognizes - including other Aberrants. Basically small, seemingly disconnected bits that don't fit, that indicate something weird. Something <i>other</i>. <br /> <br /> And as things come together the characters slowly realize that they're dealing with a new power - or, really, a very old power. That some of their enemies are part of that power. That some of their <i>allies</i> are part of that power (&quot;Of course I don't want the Aberrants to take over the Earth. I need the Earth to be intact when we eventually feed it to The Screaming Light.&quot;) That others of their enemies might be their (temporary, conditional) allies (It's not like Sandoval Gutierrez wants the Earth to be fed to The Screaming Light or any other paradimensional horror - especially while he's on it) Figure a lot of things dealing with monsters and agent with the occasional need to prevent somebody from bringing, say, The Needful Abyss to Earth to sate its hunger on... London or something. The eventual idea would be for the character to learn, grow strong and perhaps achieve Tier 3.<br /> <br /> Then they can visit The Screaming Light and the Needful Abyss to kick <i>their </i>furniture around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T00:43:19-08:00","id":1348182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1345858-what-do-we-want-next?p=1348100#post1348100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll try to find it. To be fair, I don't want to specifically use Lovecraft's Mythos simply because of how over used it already is. I want to integrate cosmic horror elements into Trinity to a certain extent but I don't want it to become Cthulhu Calls to Trinity or something especially not at first. For one thing, there's plenty of cool other stuff in Trinity. For another, Trinity is about Hope and Optimism. Lovecraft's cosmology is about as hopeless/depressing as you can get.<br /> <br /> A lot of it would be hints, clues, indications. The sub-Aberrant that doesn't seem to be part of any known Aberrant. The biotech lab whose &quot;bio&quot; seems really freaky. The intternet/opnet meme that really does seem to be driving people to kill - or do other things. The Aberrant cult centered on an &quot;Aberrant&quot; nobody recognizes - including other Aberrants. Basically small, seemingly disconnected bits that don't fit, that indicate something weird. Something <i>other</i>.<br /> <br /> And as things come together the characters slowly realize that they're dealing with a new power - or, really, a very old power. That some of their enemies are part of that power. That some of their <i>allies</i> are part of that power (&quot;Of course I don't want the Aberrants to take over the Earth. I need the Earth to be intact when we eventually feed it to The Screaming Light.&quot;) That others of their enemies might be their (temporary, conditional) allies (It's not like Sandoval Gutierrez wants the Earth to be fed to The Screaming Light or any other paradimensional horror - especially while he's on it) Figure a lot of things dealing with monsters and agent with the occasional need to prevent somebody from bringing, say, The Needful Abyss to Earth to sate its hunger on... London or something. The eventual idea would be for the character to learn, grow strong and perhaps achieve Tier 3.<br /> <br /> Then they can visit The Screaming Light and the Needful Abyss to kick <i>their </i>furniture around.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is awesome stuff. I really like the hints you're suggesting there, especially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}